1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 { The Philidor: Black supports e5 with a pawn and plays for a solid, flexible setup. }
3. d4 Nf6 { [%name Lion / Hanham] Keeping the e5 point and preparing ...Nbd7. }
( 3... exd4 { [%name 3...exd4] Giving up the centre for free piece play. }
  4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Be7 6. Be2 O-O 7. O-O Re8 { The rook pressures e4 and Black prepares ...Bf8 and ...c6 or ...a6. } )
4. Nc3 { White keeps the tension and develops. }
( 4. dxe5 { [%name 4.dxe5] White opens the centre at once. }
  4... Nxe4 5. Qd5 Nc5 6. Bg5 Be7 7. exd6 Qxd6 8. Nc3 { Black is fine after trading queens or developing with ...c6. } )
4... Nbd7 5. Bc4 Be7 { Black covers f7 and prepares to castle. }
6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 c6 8. a4 { The typical Hanham structure: Black waits for ...b6, ...Bb7 or ...exd4 and ...Re8. } *
